#heading(level: 1)[Applications to the Calculation of Double Series \
  and Integrals] <ch:double-series>

#source(173)
In this chapter we present applications of local residues to the solution of
certain problems connected with the investigation and calculation of double
series and integrals. In these problems the series under investigation admit
representations as integrals of rational functions (forms) in two variables over
two-dimensional contours. The applications will be based on the fact that by the
Cauchy-Poincaré theorem the original contour of integration is replaced by the
sum of the simplest local cycles and the original integral by the sum of local
residues. We use mainly the results of §§@sec:representability[n],
@sec:parameter[n].
